Z||000018||rogergarrison||06-24-2001||08:55 PM||||if its automatic, could be a bad neutral switch, if standard, bad clutch switch. Just something else to check if starter is OK. My minivan w/auto just stopped starting the other day, but would start when i jumped the starter. found out the two mounting screws for the neutral switch had both fell out. Replaced them, works perfect again.||||reg||1
Z||000019||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-24-2001||09:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrgone:<BR><B>could that shorting out cause my fuse to blow?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yep.. It could be grounding out.<P>||||reg||1
